WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.205
File uploads are security-sensitive because they cross a major trust boundary.

2
00:00:05.205 --> 00:00:16.483
A user, partner, integration, administrator, or background import sends content that the application did not create and cannot fully understand at the moment it arrives.

3
00:00:16.483 --> 00:00:21.755
Even when the user is authenticated, the uploaded file is still external input.

4
00:00:21.755 --> 00:00:25.159
Accepting a file is different from trusting a file.

5
00:00:25.159 --> 00:00:26.494
An ASP.

6
00:00:26.494 --> 00:00:34.035
NET Core endpoint may receive a profile photo, support attachment, invoice, CSV import, report, or product image.

7
00:00:34.035 --> 00:00:40.174
That only means the request reached the application and met the first set of handling rules.

8
00:00:40.174 --> 00:00:48.716
It does not mean the file is appropriate for preview, processing, public access, long-term storage, or download by another user.

9
00:00:48.716 --> 00:00:51.986
Upload workflows affect many parts of the system.

10
00:00:51.986 --> 00:01:07.469
They touch request handling, temporary storage, permanent storage, background processing, scanning, preview generation, imports, search indexing, downloads, administrator tools, support workflows, retention, backups, and monitoring.

11
00:01:07.469 --> 00:01:11.539
A weak assumption in one step can create problems in another.

12
00:01:11.539 --> 00:01:12.874
ASP.

13
00:01:12.874 --> 00:01:23.018
NET Core gives developers useful request-handling features, model binding, form limits, streaming options, configuration hooks, and middleware patterns.

14
00:01:23.018 --> 00:01:36.431
Those features help, but application design still controls what file categories are allowed, where files are stored, which identities can access them, how they are processed, and when they are deleted.

15
00:01:36.431 --> 00:01:42.905
Secure upload handling connects prevention, detection, privacy, reliability, and maintainability.

16
00:01:42.905 --> 00:01:47.376
Prevention limits what the application accepts and where it can go.

17
00:01:47.376 --> 00:01:50.245
Detection records events and state changes.

18
00:01:50.245 --> 00:01:53.916
Privacy controls what metadata and content are exposed.

19
00:01:53.916 --> 00:01:58.454
Reliability prevents large or slow uploads from harming the service.

20
00:01:58.454 --> 00:02:04.460
Maintainability keeps the workflow understandable enough to review as requirements change.
